WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.340
If you like horror movies that play like thrill
rides, then you're gonna love Annabelle Comes

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:05.240
Home.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.360
In this Conjuring spinoff, the gloves come
off the ghosts in a way the franchise has

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:10.760
never attempted before.

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.540
If you got lost in the chaos, here's what
went down in the closing minutes.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:18.640
Before getting into the ending, let's revisit
some important details.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.000
"Nice doll."

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:21.300
"That's what you think."

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:26.440
As most would guess from her messed-up mug,
Annabelle is obviously a haunted doll.

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:31.039
But the haunting works in a specific way,
leaving her more or less devoid of personality

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:36.460
especially compared to her haunted doll compatriots
in the Child's Play and, uh, Toy Story series.

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.720
While the doll can give off the impression
of possession, Annabelle isn't really a character

00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:44.940
of her own she's more like Billy from James
Wan's own Saw series, serving as a mascot

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:46.860
and tool for the true forces of evil.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.020
Rather than having consciousness herself,
she serves as what Lorraine Warren calls a

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:56.280
beacon for other spirits, essentially boosting
the wi-fi signal for any ghosts in its vicinity.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:01.180
This makes her very useful for ghosts and
demons, and uniquely deadly to living people.

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.480
Vulture described Annabelle Comes Home as
the Avengers: Endgame of the Conjuring Universe.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:11.420
But it's really more of a Suicide Squad, introducing
a whole team at once in the hopes that maybe

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.060
one or two of them will get their own spinoff
down the line.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.700
With the adult Warrens out of town, their
dangerous artifact room is left under the

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.869
care of just two people their daughter Judy,
and a babysitter named Mary Ellen.

00:01:21.869 --> 00:01:26.249
The duo is joined by Daniela, a friend of
Mary Ellen's, as well as Bob, a guitar-playing

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:29.700
grocer's son who has a crush on Mary Ellen,
and vice versa.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.539
Despite having little experience with the
paranormal, beyond Judy's developing gift

00:01:33.539 --> 00:01:37.859
for seeing dead people, these four end up
being the only line of defense against a world's

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:42.340
worth of demonic forces once Annabelle starts
taking control in the artifact room.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:47.619
The party kicks off after Daniela is manipulated
into opening the case of chapel glass that

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:51.000
contains Annabelle, despite countless locks
and warning signs.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.459
But there's a sympathetic motivation behind
this destructive act, with Daniela only barging

00:01:55.459 --> 00:01:59.749
into the artifact room out of a misguided
desire to reconnect with her late father,

00:01:59.749 --> 00:02:02.600
whose death in a car accident she feels responsible
for.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:06.980
Out of this desire, she ends up vulnerable
to demonic manipulation, opening the doll's

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:08.880
case and forgetting to secure it.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.060
"What else did you touch?"

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.120
"Everything."

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:18.160
Similar to the previous Annabelle movies,
the ultimate goal of the main demon in charge

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:23.010
is to acquire a soul, and part of attaining
this goal apparently involves scaring everybody

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:27.459
into submission with a squad of ghosts and
demons, newly awakened thanks to Annabelle's

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:28.460
magic touch.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.480
One of the new entities is the frightening
Ferryman, a collector of souls who's purportedly

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.800
in charge of shepherding newly-dead people
into the great beyond.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.920
His telltale sign is the rattling of coins
that he's collected, coins being the currency

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.640
by which people reach the afterlife.

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.920
In the tradition of ambiguous origin that
the movie establishes, the coins are placed

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.840
over the eyes of dead people, allowing them
to be hauled away to the great beyond.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:55.439
Unfortunately for these lost souls, the Ferryman
also seems to have a tendency to use these

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:59.920
cadavers as props, setting up macabre scenes
before bursting into frame for a big jump

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:00.920
scare.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.800
Despite bearing a resemblance to the Weeping
Woman of the sixth Conjuring universe movie,

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:10.300
The Curse of La Llorona this movie's white
dress entity represents a whole new threat.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.980
The haunted dress influences those who wear
it to kill, apparently using one former wearer

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.440
as a demonic avatar.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:20.640
Daniela has a pointed encounter with the bride
during the movie's climax, getting the sharp

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.240
end of a knife stuck in her gut.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.820
This is a fakeout, promptly revealed to have
caused no physical damage, but the reality

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.200
of what happens is arguably worse.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.060
The bride vomits gore onto Daniela, and then
essentially possesses her.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.940
The next time we see Daniela, she's wearing
the dress, and ready to kill.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:40.660
She's only stopped by the timely deployment
of some footage of the Warrens performing

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:41.540
an exorcism.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:45.659
Apparently, the recording is close enough
to the real thing that the entity inside Daniela

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.660
can't tell the difference, and the Bride is
cast out of her in a cloud of smoke.

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:54.240
Speaking of dark spectral clouds, there's
another monster we have to talk about The

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:59.920
Black Shuck, aka the Hellhound, or, as the
movie's credits refer to it, simply the werewolf.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.040
If Annabelle Comes Home is the Conjuring universe's
answer to an Avengers movie, then this over-the-top

00:04:05.049 --> 00:04:07.840
CGI monstrosity is basically the movie's Hulk.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:12.079
While the other entities seem to have some
lore explaining their motivations, this demon

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:15.440
dog appears out of nowhere, seemingly just
wanting to kill everybody.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:19.920
While the movie's monster is based on a real
legend in the Black Shuck, this ghostly canine

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:24.520
seems to be taking some influence from another
real "case" of the Warrens' — this one involving

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:28.370
their encounter with the Southend Werewolf,
which they turned into a "nonfiction" book,

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.580
Werewolf: A Demonic Possession.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:35.360
The endgame kicks in when the kids realize
that the only way to stop the madness is to

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.780
seal Annabelle back in her case the last thing
the demon controlling the doll wants.

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:43.500
The doll is retrieved from its hiding place
in the house by Mary Ellen, who braves an

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.940
encounter with the Ferryman to get the doll
to Judy.

00:04:45.940 --> 00:04:49.660
Once Judy gets her hands on Annabelle, she
rushes back to the artifact room to re-contain

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:50.660
the evil.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:54.860
Just as Judy is preparing to seal the doll
back into the glass case, she is brutally

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:59.100
attacked by the form of the actual demon who's
using Annabelle to hunt down a soul.

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:04.139
The demon immediately begins to steal Judy's
soul, only being stopped by a conveniently-placed

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:05.040
crucifix.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:09.660
But the fight isn't over backing up the lead
demon, all of the monstrous entities converge

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:12.260
on the Warrens' artifact room for one final
battle.

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:17.420
Judy is then joined by Mary Ellen and a newly-exorcised
Daniela, who work together to bat back all

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.740
of the monsters and seal Annabelle away.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:23.800
They barely succeed, and probably wouldn't
have survived the night If not for Judy's

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.900
aptitude for dealing with the undead.

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:31.100
Empowered by prayer and armed with a cross,
the preteen goes beast mode, effectively channeling

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:35.220
her mom's Catholic badassery, looking upon
the specters of the dead and saying:

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.460
"Not today."

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:41.200
After returning home and hearing the story,
the Warrens throw a small party for Judy,

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.160
to celebrate both her birthday and the continuing
survival of her mortal soul.

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.020
Joining the family are Mary Ellen, Bob, and
Daniela.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:52.690
In a surprise twist, Daniela is revealed to
have had a stern talk with her Judy-bullying

00:05:52.690 --> 00:05:56.419
brother, who led the charge at school in making
fun of Judy's paranormal home life.

00:05:56.419 --> 00:06:00.580
Thanks to this talk, a whole parade of fellow
students also shows up to the party, having

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.500
decided as a group to stop bullying the ghost
girl.

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:07.860
At this point, it's fair to wonder if the
demon is still causing hallucinations, because

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.260
that is not how school really works.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:15.080
The movie wraps up where the chaos all began,
back in the Warrens' artifact room.

00:06:15.080 --> 00:06:20.120
This time, Lorraine is accompanying Daniela
in a one-on-one chat or rather, one-on-one

00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:20.900
plus one.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:25.000
Daniela's earlier attempts to reach her father
on the other side were always doomed to be

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:28.160
fruitless without the help of an actual medium,
like Lorraine.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:32.831
On her own, all her pleas to see her dad again
only showed the demon a handy weak spot, with

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:35.840
the evil entity using the face of her father
to manipulate her.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:40.660
With Lorraine back in the mix, Daniela is
able to easily connect with her darling dad,

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:43.400
who expresses his undying love for her through
Lorraine.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:47.940
It's a well-done way to absolve Daniela of
any guilt, both for the part she feels she

00:06:47.940 --> 00:06:52.220
played in her dad's death, and her role in
unleashing the horrors of the artifact room.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:56.699
She both learns and grows from her mistake,
while also receiving the emotional resolution

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:57.840
she's been looking for.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.159
With the evil contained, Annabelle Comes Home
concludes as a rare horror movie with a happy

00:07:02.159 --> 00:07:06.010
ending though if we know this series at all,
we can bet we'll be seeing some of those new

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:08.300
monsters in their own spin offs one day soon.

